From: written for wine-mac-builds (not in Sikarugir). Second Chance does
 the same in the parent before exec today.
Upstream: no (candidate, kept on Second Chance's list for later)
Why: Mach task exception ports are inherited across fork and exec. When
 the program that starts Wine has a task-level crash handler (Sentry,
 Crashpad), faults in the Wine process go to it rather than becoming the
 signals Wine's exception handling is built on, and a Windows program hangs
 at its third fault. ntdll now clears the ports for bad access, bad
 instruction and arithmetic exceptions when it sets up signal handling,
 except under a debugger (P_TRACED), which uses them.
Status: built in macfixes-10.0-build2 and macfixes-11.21-build1; behaviour not yet tested on its own (2026-11-15).
Applies to: wine 11.21 (macfixes, after 0041)
Port to 11.21: same code; called at the start of signal_init_process( TEB * ), which 11.21 already includes <sys/sysctl.h> for.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
index 3a38af0..9553ebf 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/signal_x86_64.c
@@ -3096,6 +3096,35 @@ static int libc_addr_cb( struct dl_phdr_info *info, size_t info_size, void *arg
 }
 #endif
 
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+/***********************************************************************
+ *           clear_inherited_exception_ports
+ *
+ * Task exception ports are inherited across fork and exec. If the program
+ * that started Wine set some (a crash reporter such as Sentry or
+ * Crashpad), the Mach exceptions for faults go to that handler instead of
+ * becoming the signals Wine's fault handling depends on, and a Windows
+ * program that relies on its own exception handling hangs. Clear them, so
+ * faults always become signals. Not while a debugger is attached (it
+ * receives exceptions through these ports).
+ * Not in Sikarugir; written for wine-mac-builds.
+ */
+static void clear_inherited_exception_ports(void)
+{
+    struct kinfo_proc info;
+    size_t size = sizeof(info);
+    int mib[4] = { CTL_KERN, KERN_PROC, KERN_PROC_PID, getpid() };
+    kern_return_t kr;
+
+    info.kp_proc.p_flag = 0;
+    if (!sysctl( mib, 4, &info, &size, NULL, 0 ) && (info.kp_proc.p_flag & P_TRACED)) return;
+    kr = task_set_exception_ports( mach_task_self(),
+                                   EXC_MASK_BAD_ACCESS | EXC_MASK_BAD_INSTRUCTION | EXC_MASK_ARITHMETIC,
+                                   MACH_PORT_NULL, EXCEPTION_DEFAULT, THREAD_STATE_NONE );
+    if (kr != KERN_SUCCESS) WARN_(seh)( "task_set_exception_ports failed: %d\n", kr );
+}
+#endif
+
 /**********************************************************************
  *		signal_init_process
  */
@@ -3105,6 +3134,10 @@ void signal_init_process( TEB *teb )
     WOW_TEB *wow_teb = get_wow_teb( teb );
     void *ptr;
 
+#ifdef __APPLE__
+    clear_inherited_exception_ports();
+#endif
+
     if (user_shared_data->XState.Size) xstate_size = user_shared_data->XState.Size - sizeof(XSAVE_FORMAT);
     frame_size = offsetof( struct syscall_frame, xstate ) + xstate_size;
     xstate_extended_features = user_shared_data->XState.EnabledFeatures & ~(UINT64)3;
